  "verbalization": "Clematernoside D is implicated in the target relationship with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Clematernoside D acts as a target for several compounds, including Kaempferol 7-O-rutinoside and Bisnorstriatol, which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This indicates a potential regulatory network where Clematernoside D may influence the activity of these proteins through the intermediacy of other compounds. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with some evidence pointing to direct interactions, while others highlight indirect pathways. The integration of these findings implies that Clematernoside D may modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving the regulation of gene expression or chromatin modification. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Clematernoside D could influence the function of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
